> I don't think playwright is ready to be bundled, what is your use case?

I might've misspoken by calling it a bundler, as I don't think it's bundling in this context.

The use case is using Playwright on the server in a Remix app ~(could be Next.js or any other modern web framework)~. It's been working fine like this for as long as I can remember, it just stopped with 1.48.0 yesterday. :P

There's a comment right above the offending import:

```
// Chrome doesn't support Bidi, we create Bidi over CDP which is used by Chrome driver.
// bidiOverCdp depends on chromium-bidi which we only have in devDependencies, so
// we load bidiOverCdp dynamically.
const bidiTransport = await require('./bidiOverCdp').connectBidiOverCdp(transport); 
```

Dynamically imported or not, wouldn't bidiOverCdp's dependencies (`chromium-bidi`) need to be installed in consuming projects? Unless maybe there's a check elsewhere in the calling code to only load bidiChromium.ts if developing locally within the Playwright project, but if there is - it doesn't appear to be working.

As long as the method is not called (which it isn't), it shouldn't be an issue. Sounds like the next bundler pre-processes the code and pulls requires to the top level.

```js
  override async connectToTransport(transport: ConnectionTransport, options: BrowserOptions): Promise<BidiBrowser> {
    // Chrome doesn't support Bidi, we create Bidi over CDP which is used by Chrome driver.
    // bidiOverCdp depends on chromium-bidi which we only have in devDependencies, so
    // we load bidiOverCdp dynamically.
    const bidiTransport = await require('./bidiOverCdp').connectBidiOverCdp(transport);
    (transport as any)[kBidiOverCdpWrapper] = bidiTransport;
    return BidiBrowser.connect(this.attribution.playwright, bidiTransport, options);
  }
```

> Marking `chromium-bidi` as [external](https://esbuild.github.io/api/#external) in ESBuild might make it work.

I tried something like that but apparently I used the wrong option. This did work, though:

```
// vite.config.ts

optimizeDeps: {
  exclude: ['chromium-bidi']
},
```

[Vite's dependency pre-bundling optimization](https://vite.dev/guide/dep-pre-bundling) is what was asking esbuild to resolve chromium-bidi.

Could you guys reopen this issue. It has not been fixed.

