  rollupConfig: {
    external: ['playwright-core'],
  },
```

> Closing as per above. Not sure if it is worth bringing up with the esbuild / vite folks to let them know that they could do a better job at detecting playwright as a server-side only import.

@pavelfeldman is this the end of the story? I've tried externalizing [as described above](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/33031#issuecomment-2525655565) as well as `optimizeDeps` but there doesn't appear to be a way around this when utilizing Vite.

For what it's worth, I also get the same error when trying to run my built Nuxt app via Cloudflare's `wrangler` CLI

This worked for me:

`vite.config.js`

```js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';

export default defineConfig({
  build: {
    rollupOptions: {
      external: [
        'playwright',
        'playwright-core'
      ]
    }
  },
  optimizeDeps: {
    exclude: ['chromium-bidi']
  }
});
```
